{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794566103801,"sessionID":"ses_e2b88e085fferNVOt0Nxr9mDX0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4799a46001AClSw2Pv9wYX09","sessionID":"ses_e2b88e085fferNVOt0Nxr9mDX0","messageID":"msg_1d4798e25001VuuvjTNtcIs5RW","type":"tool","id":"call_50b371c59f404813a57e8863","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Output keys: one JSON object holds `rows`, then `liveRows`, `totalBytes`, `medianBytes`, `maxBytes`, `medianHeadBytes` and `maxHeadBytes`. Each entry of `rows` carries `id`, `bytes`, `headBytes`, `estimatedTokens` and `live`, where bytes are the UTF-8 length of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`, headBytes is the UTF-8 length of its first line, live says whether that first line starts `Advisor: live`, and tokens divide the context bytes by four, the renderer's own characters per token. Every byte statistic is taken over live rows only.\n- Refusal: a run with no live head prints `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}` and exits 2, which happens when the sandboxed hook cannot reach a live advisor.\n- Sandbox:","oldString":"- Output keys: one JSON object holds `rows`, then `totalBytes`, `medianBytes` and `maxBytes`. Each entry of `rows` carries `id`, `bytes` and `estimatedTokens`, where bytes are the UTF-8 length of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` and tokens divide that by four, the renderer's own characters per token.\n- Sandbox:","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n@@ -94,9 +94,10 @@\n \n `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` reports what the Claude prompt hook actually sends the model for a typed row.\n \n - Flags: `node measure-brief-cost.mjs [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` keeps every typed row on the `none` split, `--rows` narrows the run to named corpus ids and `--root` names the checkout the corpus and hook are read from, defaulting to the current directory. A holdout or unknown id exits 2 before anything is spawned, and no prompt is ever printed.\n-- Output keys: one JSON object holds `rows`, then `totalBytes`, `medianBytes` and `maxBytes`. Each entry of `rows` carries `id`, `bytes` and `estimatedTokens`, where bytes are the UTF-8 length of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` and tokens divide that by four, the renderer's own characters per token.\n+- Output keys: one JSON object holds `rows`, then `liveRows`, `totalBytes`, `medianBytes`, `maxBytes`, `medianHeadBytes` and `maxHeadBytes`. Each entry of `rows` carries `id`, `bytes`, `headBytes`, `estimatedTokens` and `live`, where bytes are the UTF-8 length of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`, headBytes is the UTF-8 length of its first line, live says whether that first line starts `Advisor: live`, and tokens divide the context bytes by four, the renderer's own characters per token. Every byte statistic is taken over live rows only.\n+- Refusal: a run with no live head prints `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}` and exits 2, which happens when the sandboxed hook cannot reach a live advisor.\n - Sandbox: the run makes one `ssa-cost-` directory under the OS temp dir and sets `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to it for every hook process, so the operator's warm daemon is never reached. At the end it stops only a process whose command line names that directory and removes it.\n \n ---\n \n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Output keys: one JSON object holds `rows`, then `liveRows`, `totalBytes`, `medianBytes`, `maxBytes`, `medianHeadBytes` and `maxHeadBytes`. Each entry of `rows` carries `id`, `bytes`, `headBytes`, `estimatedTokens` and `live`, where bytes are the UTF-8 length of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`, headBytes is the UTF-8 length of its first line, live says whether that first line starts `Advisor: live`, and tokens divide the context bytes by four, the renderer's own characters per token. Every byte statistic is taken over live rows only.\\n- Refusal: a run with no live head prints `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"degraded_brief\\\",...}` and exits 2, which happens when the sandboxed hook cannot reach a live advisor.\\n- Sandbox:\",\"oldString\":\"- Output keys: one JSON object holds `rows`, then `totalBytes`, `medianBytes` and `maxBytes`. Each entry of `rows` carries `id`, `bytes` and `estimatedTokens`, where bytes are the UTF-8 length of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` and tokens divide that by four, the renderer's own characters per token.\\n- Sandbox:\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794566101574,"end":1794566103801}}}}
