{"type":"text","timestamp":1794566133124,"sessionID":"ses_e2b88e085fferNVOt0Nxr9mDX0","part":{"id":"prt_1d47a019d002kbwt5iwH5H3W8Y","sessionID":"ses_e2b88e085fferNVOt0Nxr9mDX0","messageID":"msg_1d479edea001poa7BjMLlB30G6","type":"text","text":"T025 is done. I edited only the routing-accuracy README, added all eight keys the task names, and the verify command prints 8.\n\n**File written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`\n\n**What changed**\n1. The `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` row now describes `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` and `needsModeRows`, including that the label appears only when the prompt names the hub that tops the row.\n2. The `score-command-transcripts.mjs` row now says `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not. `unsafeNoChangedPath` is in the key list after `unsafe`, is defined as the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path apart from a loop without init, and the git-ignored or reverted-write sentence was added.\n3. The `### Measure the brief cost` output-keys bullet names `headBytes` and `live` per row, `liveRows`, `medianHeadBytes` and `maxHeadBytes` in the summary, and states that every byte statistic is taken over live rows only. A new Refusal bullet names the `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}` output and exit 2.\n\n**Verify output** (exit 0)\n```\n$ rg -o \"needs_mode_floor|needsModeRows|unsafeNoChangedPath|headBytes|liveRows|medianHeadBytes|degraded_brief|git-ignored\" $RAR | sort -u | wc -l\n       8\n```\nThe sorted unique matches were `degraded_brief`, `git-ignored`, `headBytes`, `liveRows`, `medianHeadBytes`, `needs_mode_floor`, `needsModeRows`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`.\n\n`git status --short` for that path shows only ` M .../routing-accuracy/README.md`. The three other modified scripts in the worktree (`measure-brief-cost.mjs`, `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs`) were already dirty from other workers and I did not touch them. No spec path, phase number, task id or rank id was added to the file, and the checkbox in `tasks.md` is untouched.\n\nSKILL ROUTING: sk-doc (advisor 0.8792) → sk-create-readme mode, loaded before the first write\nARTIFACT: sk-doc → sk-create-readme (existing code README content edit)\nREPO RULES: communication.md, communication-handoff.md, evidence-and-proof.md, scope-discipline.md\n\nNothing is the operator's to do. T025 is ready to tick, and the git state is uncommitted by design.","time":{"start":1794566128029,"end":1794566133124}}}
